    "subtopic_id": "science/grade_06/ch_10/H008",
    "stem": "Qasim sees mosquito larvae in stagnant water. A thin, transparent kerosene layer covers the water surface and blocks contact between the water and air. Adult mosquitoes fly above the water.",
    "item_type": "three_statement",
    "options": {},
    "statements": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "text": "Larvae need to reach air at the surface to breathe, so the kerosene layer disrupts their development."
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "text": "Adult mosquitoes flying above the water must also breathe through that water surface, so the layer stops them the same way."
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "text": "Because the kerosene layer is transparent, air still reaches the larvae and breathing is unchanged."
      }
